            <value>
               <exData contentType="text/html">
                  <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="font-size:18pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0in"><span style="xfa-tab-count:5">                                             </span><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">  </span><span style="text-decoration:underline">10_12 11_12 Pay Plan</span></p><p style="font-size:18pt;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:16pt;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in">Introduction:</p><p style="font-size:16pt;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">An eligible 12-month employee can request to participate in a 10/12 or 11/12 Pay Plan based</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">on the respective Collective Bargaining Agreement (CBA). An individual will receive an</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">annual salary for working 10 months or 11 months, depending on the Pay Plan, in 12</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">(twelve) salary warrants. Please read your CBA or contact Human Resource Services if you</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">have any questions.</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:16pt;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in">Instructions:<br/><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">• Complete this form in the order indicated. Please indicate the effective date and the</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">month(s) off.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="font-weight:bold">The effective date should be the beginning of a pay period.</span></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">• Your appropriate administrator will recommend and approve your request. The form will</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">then be forwarded to Human Resource Services.</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">• Human Resource Services will notify the employee and the department with the new</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">monthly salary based on the Pay Plan. At this time, the employee may elect to confirm or</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">rescind this request.</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in">Cancellation:<span style="text-decoration:none"> To terminate your 10/12 or 11/12 Pay Plan, this form should be completed.<br/>The University may also cancel your Pay Plan due to program needs and according to the<br/>respective CBA.</span></p></body>
               </exData>
